### ERROR HANDLING

**Error 1: User Provides Invalid Name**
```python
# User: "Juan123"
respond_in_user_language(
    es="❌ El nombre no debe contener números. Por favor, proporciona tu nombre completo:\n"
       "Ejemplo: Juan Pérez",
    en="❌ The name should not contain numbers. Please provide your full name:\n"
       "Example: John Smith"
)
```

**Error 2: User Provides Invalid Phone**
```python
# User: "123"
respond_in_user_language(
    es="❌ El número de teléfono es demasiado corto. Por favor, proporciona un número válido:\n"
       "Ejemplo: +52 123 456 7890\n"
       "O escribe 'omitir' si prefieres no proporcionarlo.",
    en="❌ The phone number is too short. Please provide a valid number:\n"
       "Example: +1 123 456 7890\n"
       "Or type 'skip' if you prefer not to provide it."
)
```

**Error 3: Database Error During Creation**
```python
# create_user returns success=False
respond_in_user_language(
    es="❌ Hubo un error técnico al crear tu cuenta.\n"
       "Por favor, intenta de nuevo en unos momentos.\n\n"
       "Si el problema persiste, contacta a soporte.",
    en="❌ There was a technical error creating your account.\n"
       "Please try again in a few moments.\n\n"
       "If the problem persists, contact support."
)
```

**Error 4: User Already Exists (Edge Case)**
```python
# This shouldn't happen if authentication_flow is followed correctly
# But handle it gracefully if check_user_exists was not called

if "already exists" in error_message.lower():
    respond_in_user_language(
        es="Parece que ya tienes una cuenta registrada con este correo.\n"
           "Voy a cargar tu información existente.",
        en="It seems you already have an account registered with this email.\n"
           "I'll load your existing information."
    )

    # Fetch user data and proceed to welcome menu
    user_data = check_user_exists(email=validated_email)
    proceed_to_welcome_menu(user_data)
```

